id: pm-starter-ci-v2
title: Apply Fleet CI v2 with quick PR gates and exhaustive deep validation
description: "Companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Preserve required check names, all existing release-gate contracts and starter copy workflows; add deterministic quick depth and bounded deep jobs without modifying release rollout files."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: ci,performance
created_at: "2026-11-15T14:10:20.191Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T20:10:10.255Z"
assignee: codex-sol-round-d
claim_principal: codex-sol-round-d
author: codex-sol
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-15T14:10:23.797Z",codex-sol,"Required checks are test (22) and test (26); CodeQL is optional. No open CI or flaky-gate item was found. Latest successful main run 43681245615: Node 22 npm/Bun gates 64s/61s, Node 26 56s/55s. Individual job log fallback was needed because gh run view --log returned empty. Slowest corpus is the 500-sequence recipes property (16.10s), followed by CLI acceptance (11.76s) and pagination property (5.30s). Preserve current coverage scope and thresholds and every old check in the tier inventory."
  "2026-11-15T14:11:38.135Z",codex-sol,"Clone-based scaffolding already inherits the repository tree; README now explicitly retains ci.yml, ci-deep.yml, codeql.yml and test/support/depth.ts. The setup wizard returns scaffolded:false and does not generate a second package, so no generator is invented. Four 500-case property/arithmetic corpora use the same 50-case deterministic prefix; fixed pagination-boundary fixtures remain unchanged. Standalone validate-consumer-pack proves Bun global and bunx host paths but is not part of release:check, so PRs retain explicit Bun install and bunx local-bin smoke. Deep certifies npm and fresh Bun graphs on Node 22/26."
  "2026-11-15T14:14:01.239Z",codex-sol,"Initial quick touched-file batch passes 31/31 in 59.73s. Canonical lint found a pre-existing literal sparse-array adversarial fixture; expressed the identical hole-bearing fixture with Object.assign(Array(3), indices) so lint can pass without weakening refusal coverage. This package has no lint script/parser peers; used an existing external canonical pm-ops lint installation read-only. Strict health initially found a CLI/extension host version mismatch; install the already-declared pm-github 2026.10.4 project extension before health in both tiers to remove ambient host resolution. The managed registry is restored after provisioning."
  "2026-11-15T14:15:11.453Z",codex-sol,"Pre-push: typecheck, test compilation, build, strict YAML and tier invariants pass. Canonical lint passes all six changed TypeScript files after preserving the sparse fixture without a literal hole. Strict health now passes after project-owned extension provisioning. Quick touched-file run passes 31/31 in 59.73s; one quick coverage run is in progress with unchanged 100/100/100 thresholds and a 20-minute bound. Full depth is reserved for deep CI."
  "2026-11-15T14:17:22.269Z",codex-sol,"One PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick npm run coverage passes in 94.26s linked-command wall, with all seven configured sources reported and unchanged 100% lines, branches and functions. Existing deterministic cases already cover the quick prefix at the original thresholds; no source exclusions or threshold reductions were needed. Quick touched files pass 31/31 in 59.73s; typecheck, build:test, build, canonical lint, strict YAML, changelog, strict health, identity audits and Bun/bunx smoke pass. Full baseline gates were 55-64s on hosted hardware; these are different-host observations, not a controlled speedup. Full local depth and standalone global/ephemeral packed acceptance were not run. PR #215 initial CI 43723404900 and CodeQL 43723405034 are queued, so no completed PR wall time can be measured. Final receipt head will supersede those runs. Required checks, release rollout files, repository variables and protection are unchanged. Deep and exact-head hosted CI remain unverified; claim released for orchestrator review."
  "2026-11-15T19:58:28.515Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Round D: verify PR 215 findings, preserve docs and tracker privacy gates, default starter clones to hosted deep runners, pin deep actions, and self-review all six CI defect classes. Existing required tests passed; Greptile reports SDK evidence bypass."
  "2026-11-15T20:07:48.827Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Round D fixes: documentation tier runs SDK-floor evidence tests while retaining strict health, changelog and identity/privacy audits. Deep defaults to hosted Ubuntu unless PM_LOCAL_DEEP=on, uses pinned actions and separate Node x npm/Bun jobs. Self-review also restored CodeQL eligibility for executable tracker files. Added executable classifier, input-gate, runner/matrix, action-pin and strict YAML regressions; product timeouts and seeded outcome thresholds are unchanged. No coverage source changed in this round, so coverage was not repeated."
  "2026-11-15T20:10:10.253Z",codex-sol-round-d,"Round D final local evidence: linked typecheck/build:test plus workflow/depth/SDK-floor/identity/release-workflow batch passed 20 tests in 17.76 s command wall; canonical lint for all PR tooling/test TypeScript passed (8.70 s final invocation). Strict YAML includes all root workflows. changelog:full/check and strict tracked-project health passed; health linked command passed in 30.05 s using tracker context after schema-context mismatch was refused. Thread fixes: PRRT_kwDOSZp3U863qauz, PRRT_kwDOSZp3U863qo2J, PRRT_kwDOSZp3U863qo2M. Existing PR run 43723547679 passed required Node 22/26 jobs in 54/67 s execution, with created-to-completed walls 75m49s/71m56s. Those are previous-head results; replacement-head CI is not yet verified. No thread replies, resolutions, merges or item closures."
